                <dt>Scope Note</dt><dd>Conditions characterized by disturbances of usual sleep patterns or behaviors. <a href="/record/ui?ui=D012893" class="textLink_SLEEPWAKEDISORDERS">SLEEP WAKE DISORDERS</a> may be divided into three major categories: <a href="/record/ui?ui=D020920" class="textLink_DYSSOMNIAS">DYSSOMNIAS</a> (i.e. disorders characterized by insomnia or hypersomnia), <a href="/record/ui?ui=D020447" class="textLink_PARASOMNIAS">PARASOMNIAS</a> (abnormal sleep behaviors), and <a href="/record/ui?ui=D012893" class="textLink_SLEEPWAKEDISORDERS">SLEEP WAKE DISORDERS</a> secondary to medical or psychiatric disorders. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p187)</dd>
            

